ams don't want a guy like jameis  winston to come in and be their backup  he's just too talented he's going to  make a lot of starter a lot of starters  not look as good or have guys on the  practice field scratching their head  going wait why aren't we playing him he  out duels our starter every day so  that's where it's james i mean a little  scary i think for jameis winston right  now  but why shouldn't he be the starter then  that's what's amazing to me if he's  going to come in and perform better than  the starter why isn't the team saying  this guy should be our starter and i  know for some teams the financial  commitment is too great to pivot to  someone else you're already all in with  someone else and it's going to be  incredibly expensive and there's going  to be a huge cap problem but i agree  with you you know the backup quarterback  most teams are looking for a guy who  comes in knows his role accepts his role  he's there to prepare the veteran or the  starter excuse me he's there to be the  veteran presence he's there to help the  starter he's there to nudge the starter  but he's not there to try to take the  starters job some places want that one  and two who are battling it out like the  bears this year for the most part they  want a number two who understands this  is who i am this is my role i'm only  gonna play if this guy gets injured and  uh  that makes jameis winston not an  attractive option because he's still  going to want to play and he's going to  want to show up and prove that he's the  best guy on the roster  yeah exactly right i mean well said i  mean that that's exactly right you know  and plus yeah there's going to be teams  that are going to be out there that go i  don't know if i trust them to be my  starter yet so that's a little bit of  the issue with winston to me this is the  play right here for jameis winston  you call the san francisco 49ers you  call the pittsburgh steelers you tell  them i will play for the minimum who  give